/target
# The bench crate (benches/Cargo.toml) declares its own [workspace] table,
# excluding it from the root workspace, so it builds into its own target dir
# that the bare `/target` entry above does not cover.
/benches/target
*.snap.new

# Raw profiles from a local `cargo llvm-cov` run. The wrapper writes them
# beside each crate's manifest rather than under `/target`, so the bare entry
# above does not cover them, and a coverage run leaves a dozen or more
# untracked files behind.
*.profraw

# macOS Finder droppings
.DS_Store

# Subagent task reports and the execution ledger. Working scratch: useful
# while a phase is running, noise in the history afterwards. Nine of these
# were committed by accident when Phase 14 merged.
.superpowers/
docs/teach

# examples/polyglot build artifacts: a venv and a compiled Go binary, both
# built by a setup script the docs page names, neither meant to be
# committed. .rs/.js/.py/.go SOURCE under examples/polyglot/ is tracked as
# normal; only what those two setup scripts produce is excluded here.
/examples/polyglot/venv/
/examples/polyglot/go-http/go-http
/crates/shep-cli/completions/
